 what can be fun about that game is the  open world aspect of it the kind of  chaotic i can do anything  anything goes kind of thing what is your  goal what is your tactic to kind of  funneling that into one kind of cogent  story yeah it's  so it's a tricky one right i mean i love  the franchise i've played all the games  huge fan of it  and we have a director f gary gray who's  attached to it he's an amazing  visionary director um has done some  incredible one of my some some of my  favorite films including set it off  which i still think is one of the best  oh i love said it off it's fantastic so  good  he's got a great vision for it he knows  what he wants to do i think from a story  why from a storytelling perspective it  was  you know it was two things it was it was  the the tricky things with something  like stanford is gonna be tone  right away right because you know if you  know the franchise you know that it  it's it basically had two tones it has  more of the gritty tone which is the  first couple movies and then it goes  kind of bonkers and just absolutely  insane  and so we wanted to make sure that we  weren't isolating either of those so  that so it's about it's about just  trying to find uh find the tonal balance  where you have real characters  real stakes part of it with mortal  kombat 2 it's like you wanted to you  wanted to feel real you want the  characters to feel  real as much as possible but you also  want to lean into  what made it fun and lean into that  craziness so  part of it was trying to figure out that  tone which i think it's finally gotten  into a place where  it makes sense and then it was a matter  of what kind of movie is this because  how do you take an open world movie and  tell a story so  you know i looked at different films  that i really love i'm a big fan of 70s  cinema so i looked at the warriors  uh i looked at uh escape from new york  uh  speaking the language yeah just some of  those classics and i said well how do we  how do we kind of pull from some of  those and tell our own unique story so  i'm excited for it we'll see  that's awesome so am i uh last question  for you  what is the space invaders film looking  like  ah i really this one's really really a  passion project of mine you know when i  i uh one thing that you know when i got  it  it's funny like i first felt a couple  years ago three or three actually maybe  like three four years ago  and it came to me and i was like you  know and i passed on it because i just i  couldn't figure out i did what i didn't  want to do is i didn't want to do  independence day i didn't want to do a  big alien invasion movie that i've seen  a hundred times i always try to try to  avoid that kind of stuff so  i couldn't figure it out and then it  came back around like a couple years ago  and um and i was like you know what i  gotta i gotta figure this out because i  love the original game it's the  grandfather of  video games really it was it's the still  i think one of the biggest all-time  selling games ever right in vivian  history so  um so i had to figure it out and so i  found a really unique way into it that's  all focused on character and just  emotion and  heart it sounds crazy when i'm talking  about space invaders but  i pulled a lot from my own life growing  up in new jersey and it's just this kind  of  it's just it's it's a very uh emotional  uh personal story so i hope  i hope it happens that's awesome man  thanks so much for your time congrats on  mortal kombat  thank you greg thank you my friend thank  you for taking the time
 

